fect bars on each shared-color object with the opposite panel color.\n162: \n163:     Input structure\n164:     - The grid contains two large panel colors and one shared object color.\n165:     - Each shared-color object is a mostly solid rectangle inside exactly one panel.\n166:     Rule\n167:     - Find the near-solid rectangular core of each object.\n168:     - Missing core pixels and one-cell protrusions define two-pixel bars perpendicular to the nearest core edge.\n169:     - Recolor those bars with the other panel color; leave all other pixels unchanged.\n170:     Key insight\n171:     - The colors to add are not tied to numeric ids: each object's surrounding panel identifies the opposite panel color.\n172:     \"\"\"\n173:     g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)\n174:     out = g.copy()\n175: \n176:     object_color, components, panel_colors = _object_components(g)\n177:     for coords in components:\n178:         neighbors = _neighbor_colors(g, coords, object_color)\n179:         assert len(neighbors) == 1\n180:         panel_color = next(iter(neighbors))\n181:         target_colors = panel_colors - {panel_color}\n182:         assert len(target_colors) == 1\n183:         target_color = next(iter(target_colors))\n184: \n185:         rect = _core_rect(coords)\n186:         for r, c in _defect_bar_cells(coords, rect):\n187:             assert 0 <= r < g.shape[0] and 0 <= c < g.shape[1]\n188:             assert int(g[r, c]) in {object_color, panel_color}\n189:             out[r, c] = target_color\n190: \n191:     return out\n192: \n193: # --------------- generator (att1) ---------------\n194: \n195: # Palette and canvas bounds.\n196: COLOR_IDS = list(range(10))\n197: GRID_SIZE_MIN = 20\n198: GRID_SIZE_MAX = 27\n199: \n200: # Panel layout bounds and options.\n201: MIN_PANEL_DIM = 9\n202: MIN_VISIBLE_BORDERS = 2\n203: BORDER_CHOICES = (0, 1)\n204: OFFSET_MIN = 2\n205: OFFSET_MAX = 6\n206: HORIZONTAL_LAYOUT = 0\n207: VERTICAL_LAYOUT = 1\n208: HORIZONTAL_OFFSETS = (\"le